{
  "name": "Agent Lab Calm Down email (manual, inactive, SSH transport)",
  "active": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "name": "Manual Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "id": "calm-down-0"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "fear",
              "name": "fear",
              "value": "REPLACE WITH THE FEAR TO RESEARCH",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Fear Input",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        220,
        0
      ],
      "id": "calm-down-1"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const fear = String($input.first().json.fear ?? '').trim();\nif (!fear || fear.length > 300 || /[\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f]/.test(fear)) {\n  throw new Error('fear_invalid');\n}\n// base64 contains only [A-Za-z0-9+/=], so it is inert inside the shell command below\nreturn [{ json: { fear_b64: Buffer.from(fear, 'utf8').toString('base64') } }];"
      },
      "name": "Bound And Encode Fear",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        440,
        0
      ],
      "id": "calm-down-2"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "command",
        "operation": "execute",
        "command": "=\"$AGENT_LAB_CALM_DOWN_PYTHON\" \"$AGENT_LAB_CALM_DOWN_RUNNER\" run --fear-b64 {{ $json.fear_b64 }}"
      },
      "name": "Run Research",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.ssh",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        660,
        0
      ],
      "retryOnFail": false,
      "maxTries": 1,
      "notes": "Runs only the fixed host runner over the n8n SSH node (transport per owner direction on #36). Attach the owner's SSH credential in n8n after import; none is exported. The remote login environment must define the AGENT_LAB_CALM_DOWN_* variables. Unverified end to end.",
      "id": "calm-down-3"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "research-succeeded?",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.code }}",
              "rightValue": 0,
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Research Succeeded?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        880,
        0
      ],
      "notes": "The SSH node does not fail on a non-zero exit code. A refusal from Run Research stops the workflow here (false branch is intentionally unconnected).",
      "id": "calm-down-4"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "command",
        "operation": "execute",
        "command": "=\"$AGENT_LAB_CALM_DOWN_PYTHON\" \"$AGENT_LAB_CALM_DOWN_RUNNER\" claim --execution-id {{ JSON.parse($('Run Research').first().json.stdout).execution_id }}"
      },
      "name": "Claim Delivery",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.ssh",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1100,
        0
      ],
      "retryOnFail": false,
      "maxTries": 1,
      "notes": "Runs only the fixed host runner over the n8n SSH node (transport per owner direction on #36). Attach the owner's SSH credential in n8n after import; none is exported. The remote login environment must define the AGENT_LAB_CALM_DOWN_* variables. Unverified end to end.",
      "id": "calm-down-5"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "claim-succeeded?",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.code }}",
              "rightValue": 0,
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Claim Succeeded?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        1320,
        0
